# TODO: replace the tenant ID in the GOPROXY URL below with your own Snyk tenant ID.
# BEGIN snyk-malicious-code-defense: golang
GOPROXY=https://api.au.snyk.io/hidden/tenants/8951eddb-f5c4-4564-986c-1373b4bcbc6a/registry/golang/
# END snyk-malicious-code-defense: golang

# This file is loaded explicitly via GOENV (see demo.sh) rather than written to
# Go's default user env file (`go env GOENV`, set by `go env -w`), so it only
# affects this demo's installs -- not every `go get` you run on this machine.
#
# There is deliberately no ",direct" suffix on GOPROXY: Go falls back to
# fetching straight from the VCS host when a proxy answers 404/410, which would
# silently bypass the policy this demo is showing.
#
# No token is committed here. Go reads ~/.netrc for proxy credentials, so the
# same entry the pip demo uses works for Go too:
#   machine api.au.snyk.io
#   login snyk
#   password <your Snyk token>
